\paragraph{SC failure modes and fine-grained variants.}
\citet{chen2023twofailures} identify SC failures in reasoning (hypothetical, compositional) where consistent outputs are systematically wrong; our correlation-selection gap is a distinct structured-generation failure where signals \textit{correlate} with quality yet fail to \textit{select}.
\citet{chen2024usc} extend SC to free-form tasks via universal matching; our diagnostic framework shows such extensions face limits under constrained decoding (\S\ref{sec:selection_gap}). \citet{thirukovalluru2024atomic} decompose claims into atomic units; our entity-level decomposition reveals that sub-output agreement does not translate to selection gain.

