\paragraph{SC failure modes and fine-grained variants.}
\citet{chen2023twofailures} identify SC failures where consistent outputs are systematically wrong; \citet{huang2024large} show LLMs cannot self-correct reasoning without external feedback. Our correlation-selection gap is a distinct failure where signals \textit{correlate} with quality yet fail to \textit{select}.
\citet{chen2024usc} extend SC to free-form tasks; our diagnostic shows such extensions face limits under constrained decoding (\S\ref{sec:selection_gap}). \citet{thirukovalluru2024atomic} decompose claims atomically; our entity-level decomposition reveals sub-output agreement does not translate to selection gain.

